#
# # vr5b_typed_print
#
# VR.5b — dbg boxes across the any extern ABI and narrows by spec on return
#
# ## Notes
#
# `dbg(x)` crosses the extern boundary as `fz_dbg_value(t) :: t when t: any`:
# the `any` bound still boxes typed scalar args before the call, but the
# shared variable `t` now carries the caller's argument type straight
# through the extern's own contract, so each call site's activation is
# specialized to its own return rather than borrowing an unboxing
# performed at the public wrapper. Float debug rendering is shared by
# the boxed path so `4.0` remains `4.0`.
def int_main() do
  dbg(42)
end

def float_main() do
  dbg(1.5 + 2.5)
end

def main() do
  int_main()
  float_main()
end
